      "relevant": false,
      "not_relevant_because": "The manuscript proves that a holomorphic one-parameter family of isolated surface singularities in C^3 with constant Milnor number is topologically right-trivial, which is the direction from constant Milnor number to topology; the Zariski conjecture asks whether topological equisingularity forces equal multiplicity, and the manuscript neither assumes topological equisingularity nor states or proves any multiplicity conclusion, with multiplicity entering only as a cited input (Fernández de Bobadilla–Pełka: constant Milnor number gives constant multiplicity) that already covers the μ-constant families it studies and so adds nothing to the Zariski question.",
